source_provenance.prompt:
Use case: stylized-concept
Asset type: production game enemy animation sprite atlas, 4 columns by 4 rows, exactly sixteen separate full-body animation frames, transparent PNG.
Input image 1 is the sole character identity reference. Create new animation poses of exactly this original M01 Rustfang mining monster: squat heavy nonhuman rock-and-rusted-metal industrial creature, narrow orange vertical furnace face, hooded iron head sunk into shoulders, broad chipped rusty plates with traces of ochre industrial paint, quartz chunks embedded in upper back, enormous integrated hinged pickaxe forearm and other crushing claw, short digitigrade mechanical claw legs. Maintain the reference's precise identity, proportions, realistic detailed game art, materials, wear and colors across all 16 frames. This is a monster, never a human in armor.
COMPOSITION: square 2048 x 2048 canvas. Invisible strict 4 by 4 grid of sixteen 512 x 512 cells. Do not draw grid or labels. One complete creature inside each cell, same camera, same body scale (standing foot to head about 310px), same 3/4 view FACING SCREEN RIGHT in every cell. Entire body, pickaxe tips and claw feet visible, ample transparent margins on all four sides, no pixels crossing the cell boundaries. Standing ground/foot contact point near local x=256 y=442 in every cell. The monster walks IN PLACE; center of mass stays close to this cell position. It does not traverse the atlas. Pickaxe kept away from frame boundaries even when raised. No shadows, floors, backdrops, glows outside body, text, numbers, labels, particles, flashes, action streaks or effects. Actual transparent alpha around each sprite.
Animation order row-major left to right and then top to bottom, distinct anatomical poses:
ROW 1 (frames 0,1,2,3), first half of eight frame walk cycle:
0 near claw foot forward planted and far foot back, heavy contact pose, opposite shoulder rotation;
1 near knee compresses under weight, torso down slightly, far heel lifts;
2 far leg swings through beneath pelvis, planted near foot stays behind, pickaxe counterbalances;
3 far foot reaches forward airborne, supporting ankle extends, torso rises slightly.
ROW 2 (frames 4,5,6,7), opposite half of same smooth eight frame cycle:
4 far claw foot forward planted and near foot back, opposite contact;
5 far knee compresses, near heel lifts, torso down;
6 near leg swings through pelvis, far leg supports behind;
7 near foot reaches forward airborne, supporting ankle extends, torso rises, leading smoothly back to frame 0.
The claw feet must genuinely alternate with visible knee and ankle articulation; coordinated small hip and shoulder shifts carry the massive weight. Pickaxe and claw counter-swing subtly without identity changes. Never eight copies of a static standing pose.
ROW 3 (frames 8,9,10,11), pickaxe attack sequence:
8 begin windup: grounded wide feet, torso turns back, integrated pickaxe forearm lifts diagonally overhead;
9 full anticipation: pickaxe high and back, elbow strongly bent, torso recoils ready to strike, center anchored;
10 release: a visibly different powerful downward-forward chopping pose, upper torso pitches forward, pickaxe head low ahead toward the ground, knees brace, no added impact effect;
11 recovery: pickaxe rises from low strike, torso partly straightens, weight centered again.
ROW 4 (frames 12,13,14,15), hit reaction recovery:
12 initial hit: torso and head snap back, knees soften, claw pulls inward;
13 deepest recoil/compression: shoulders lean back markedly, abdomen folds, one claw foot braces to stop imbalance, pickaxe droops;
14 regained balance: torso comes forward halfway, knees recover, pickaxe returns toward guard;
15 stable guard return: torso upright in characteristic hunched silhouette, both feet grounded, ready to walk.
There must be exactly 16 sprites, distinct continuous movement, fixed facing and consistent scale. Preserve silhouette integrity: no extra limbs, no detached tool, no new armor shapes, no human facial features. Detailed crisp production game rendering with neutral consistent top-left lighting and transparent background.
